        "Snapshot checks used exact comparisons for paused live/camera state and a 0.01-degree displayed-angle tolerance selected before these comparisons. Expected immutable captured values and atomic paused restores were observed after changing live time, speed, selection, view and playing. Restore from playing and paused states synchronized all state; repeated tracking and overview restores reproduced standard camera coordinates after camera orbit/zoom. Drag/zoom in both camera modes while paused changed camera state without changing selection, time or speed. Capacity rejected a fourth capture with unchanged list/live state; deletion preserved remaining order and IDs; recapture generated a unique replacement. Export contained exactly the versioned required fields and actual planet IDs.",
