        "Persistence checks: imported IDs/order/values survived reload while live state restarted playing, 1x, no selection and overview (observed near-zero startup readout 0.06 seconds). Deletion and capture persisted in separate reload checks. Corrupting only this artifact's storage key and reloading produced an empty list, visible recovery notice and usable controls. A temporary page-local Storage.setItem throw simulated a write failure: capture remained usable in memory and displayed saving-unavailable/unsaved-data warning. The original storage method was restored and a valid payload reimported before cleanup.",
        "Keyboard checks at the available 1600x1000 CSS viewport used actual Tab, arrow/Home keys, Enter and text typing to operate time, speed, all planet buttons, tracking/overview, capture/restore/delete, textarea editing and export/import. Enter activated buttons successfully; observed visible focus outline and sequential Tab route with no trap and no horizontal overflow. The driver's Space spelling did not activate buttons in the attempted sequence; ordinary native Space operation is therefore unverified, not claimed defective. Exact required 1440x900 and 390x844 viewport checks could not run: Page.setViewportSize is undefined and invoking it returned TypeError: not a function. No alternate browser runtime or security change was used. Mobile layout and keyboard sequences at both exact requested sizes remain unverified.",
